module DASHI.Physics.YangMills.BalabanYM4ConstrainedGaussianGaugeTransverseGramDecompositionExact where

------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ROW A1b:  GAUGE (PARALLEL) + TRANSVERSE GRAM DECOMPOSITION OF THE
--   CONSTRAINED-GAUSSIAN SECOND VARIATION
--
-- THE ROUTE THIS REPLACES.  `BalabanYM4ConstrainedGaussianFixedAmbientSecondVariationExact`
-- reduces the sign of the constrained-Gaussian shell contribution to the sign
-- of ONE Taylor coefficient `k_2` of the bordered (KKT) determinant, and
-- `BalabanYM4SignNormalizedBorderedKKTSecondVariationExact` gives the
-- sign-normalised criterion `d_1^2 > 2 d_0 d_2`.  Getting `b_- > 0` that way
-- means expanding a literal determinant and proving the sign of the resulting
-- rational number.
--
-- THE ROUTE PROVED HERE.  Split the fluctuation of the literal background into
-- a gauge/marginal part and a constrained (physical, transverse) part,
--
--     delta U  =  delta U_par  +  delta U_perp ,
--
-- which is the native background-field decomposition, and ask instead for the
-- SHAPE
--
--     D^2 S (delta U, delta U)
--        =  D^2 S_par                       (gauge / marginal channel)
--         + G(a,b)                          (transverse Gram form)
--         + R ,                             (regular remainder)
--
--     G(a,b) = |a|^2 |b|^2 - <a,b>^2 = |a ^ b|^2 .
--
-- If the gauge/marginal channel cancels exactly — which is what invariance of
-- the constrained Gaussian along the orbit/normalisation directions gives —
-- then the sign question is answered WITHOUT any determinant expansion:
--
--   * `gramPartNonNeg` : the transverse piece is nonnegative for free
--     (Lagrange's identity, `BalabanYM4GramWedgeIdentityExact`);
--   * `nonCollinearityCertificate` : it is STRICTLY positive as soon as one
--     wedge minor of the transverse pair is nonzero.  This is the sharper
--     statement: occupation of the transverse sector is not enough, the Gram
--     defect certifies non-collinearity, with the quantitative margin
--     `|a ^ b|^2`;
--   * `secondVariationFloor` / `positiveSecondVariation` : with
--     `margin <= G(a,b)` and `|R| <= rho < margin`, the second variation is at
--     least `margin - rho > 0`, which is exactly Row A's `b_-` in the form the
--     downstream gates consume.
--
-- AND THE BRIDGE BACK TO THE DETERMINANT ROUTE.  `GramShapedCoefficient` shows
-- the two routes are compatible: if the epsilon^2 coefficient `k_2` of the
-- bordered determinant is itself of Gram shape in the transverse data, then
-- `0 <= k_2` holds automatically, and the fixed-ambient criterion delivers
-- `S''(0) >= 0` — strictly positive under non-collinearity — with no sign
-- computation at all.
--
-- WHAT IS STILL INPUT (so Row A stays OPEN).
--
--   (i)   that the literal Wilson + reduced Faddeev-Popov + Haar second
--         variation admits the displayed three-term decomposition with the
--         given transverse pair (a,b);
--   (ii)  the exact cancellation of the gauge/marginal channel for the
--         constrained (not the unconstrained) Gaussian;
--   (iii) the non-collinearity margin `margin <= G(a,b)`;
--   (iv)  the remainder enclosure `|R| <= rho` (the twelve numbers counted in
--         `BalabanYM4FourOrbitRegularRemainderBudgetExact`).
--
-- None of (i)-(iv) is supplied here.  No row is closed and the frozen research
-- count stays at 4.
--
-- Exact rational arithmetic; no postulate, no hole, no receipt.  Checked with
-- `agda --safe`.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

